When trading with Central African CFA Francs (XAF) across CEMAC countries like Cameroon, Gabon, or Chad, here is exactly what "buying" and "selling" mean using your local payment methods: [1, 2] 
## 🟢 When you click "BUY" (Cash ➡️ Crypto)
You are using your hard-earned XAF cash to acquire crypto (usually USDT, Bitcoin, or FDUSD). [3, 4] 

* 
* The Process: You select an ad, enter the amount of XAF you want to spend, and get the vendor's payment details.
* Local Payment Channels: You will send the XAF via MTN Mobile Money (MoMo), Orange Money, or a local bank transfer (like UBA, Afriland First Bank, or Société Générale).
* The Result: Once you transfer the XAF and send proof, the platform's escrow releases the crypto into your wallet. [3, 5, 6] 
* 

## 🔴 When you click "SELL" (Crypto ➡️ Cash)
You are exchanging your crypto to get XAF cash sent directly to you. [4] 

* 
* The Process: You choose a buyer's ad and enter the amount of crypto you want to cash out. The platform instantly locks your crypto in escrow. [3] 
* Receiving the Funds: You sit back and wait. The buyer must send the equivalent XAF to your MoMo, Orange Money, or bank account. [4, 6] 
* The Critical Rule: Never click "Confirm Release" until you see the confirmation SMS from MTN/Orange or log into your banking app and verify that the XAF has fully cleared in your balance. [7] 
* 

